  "Question": "On a particular January day, the high temperature in Lincoln, Nebraska, was \\(16\\) degrees higher than the low temperature, and the average of the high and low temperatures was \\(3\\) degrees. What was the low temperature in Lincoln that day (in degrees)?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\( -13 \\)",
    "B": "\\( -8 \\)",
    "C": "\\( -5 \\)",
    "D": "\\( -3 \\)",
    "E": "\\( 11 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The average of two temperatures lies halfway between them. Since the high and low are \\(16\\) degrees apart, the low is \\(16\\div2=8\\) degrees below their average. Thus the low temperature was\n\\[\n3-8=\\boxed{-5\\text{ degrees}}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\text{C}\\).",
